{"title":"2026 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 13","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The mass of a serving tray <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is times the mass of a plate. A waiter is holding a serving tray with a stack of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> plates on the tray. If the combined mass of the tray and the plates is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/1/ca10728232a42354180dfd575b5c9122bd6d236a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3000 \\text{g}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"17\" />, what is the mass of each plate?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/3/eb36649bc355ce55ed96291fdac3600bebd02d13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 600 \\text{ g} \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 150 \\text{ g} \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 30 \\text{ g} \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 500 \\text{ g} \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 300 \\text{ g}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"502\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the mass of each plate. The mass of the serving tray would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/4/ed4977828049d99f20ccd3b4acb6bbd43c2eb70f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> and the mass of all the plates would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/3/2f3c6262fbacae6ba07fea6f24758dde08078e97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />. The combined mass is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/d/2edf1cf14171c36edfcf1aa32931b94f544956fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3000 \\text{ g}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" />, so:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/3/913785cbf929c3817a6b04ed423c779017276551.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4x + 6x = 3000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"124\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/1/681bd2f92dc2218495f519f14673358bdf90ad8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10x = 3000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"91\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/7/4a7658e5e13a99dffa3e1f11aa0b46a5ec915efb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{3000}{10} = \\boxed{\\textbf {(E) } 300 \\text{ g}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"187\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2026 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2026 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\"